// =============================================================================
// Chora Fog Orchestrator Service (gRPC)
// =============================================================================
//
// Source-of-truth: docs/architecture/adrs/adr-143-per-user-knowledge-graph-hexagonal-fog.md
//   + chora-contracts/proto/services/langgraph_orchestrator.proto (reference pattern)
//   + chora-contracts/proto/events/consumption/knowledge_graph.proto
//
// Inter-service gRPC contract for the per-user hexagonal exploration fog
// generation orchestrator. Implements the Python LangGraph orchestrator
// pattern per Tier 2 D5 hybrid kernel + Tier 5 D20 hybrid crew composition.
//
// Owning service: chora-fog-orchestrator (Python LangGraph + FastAPI)
//   - Path: services/chora-fog-orchestrator/
//   - StateGraph nodes: validate → assemble_context → guardrail_pre →
//                       broker_call → guardrail_post → detect_junctions →
//                       publish_events
//   - PostgresSaver checkpointer to chora_ai_kernel DB (NOT chora_consumption)
//   - Calls chora-fog-generator-executor (Go) via gRPC for stateless model
//     invocation
//
// Why a separate orchestrator (not reusing kernel RunCrew): per Tier 5 D20,
// fog gen is a domain-specialist crew (Consumption-scoped), distinct from
// the platform kernel orchestrator. Typed proto contract gives compile-time
// validation, clear SLOs (P50 < 2.5s, P99 < 6s, < $0.005 per fog), and
// team-level ownership (Team 1 + Team 3 jointly).
//
// Primary caller: chora-consumption (internal aggregate orchestration on
// HexagonRepo cache miss / stale).
//
// Idempotency: GenerateFog is idempotent on request_id (UUIDv7). Repeat
// calls within checkpoint TTL return the same result without re-invoking
// the LLM.
//
// Deployed in chora-489812 team-platform pool. mTLS via Cloud Service Mesh;
// SPIFFE identity in mesh; W3C trace context in gRPC metadata.
// =============================================================================

